  "restKeys": {
    "reason": "The same measure at each clip’s own key times (keys past a clip’s end, which neither reaches, left out). Format 1 writes a key’s time to the millisecond, so it lies up to a third of a millisecond from its frame (0.033 s for 1/30 s), 1% of a frame’s step. The worst cases are keys in the fastest swings, where that 1% is up to 35 mm: Victory’s right arm turns its twist by 175° toward the next key, so the decode itself moves 35 mm between 1.233 s and 1/30 s × 37; Sword_Regular_B’s sword arm swings into its last key, which the decode reaches at 0.533 s and the bake at its frame, 1/30 s × 16. At the frames the two agree to 5 µm.",
